---
// The genuinely-unique feature: agent automation over MCP, with segregated
// read-only and destructive registries and a hard protected-reject.

const readOnly = ["scan_status", "list_findings", "explain_rule", "preview_cleanup"];
const destructive = ["run_cleanup", "empty_trash"];
---

<section class="border-b border-edge-soft bg-void py-20 sm:py-28">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1180px] px-5 sm:px-8">
    <div class="grid gap-x-14 gap-y-10 lg:grid-cols-[0.85fr_1.15fr] lg:items-center">
      <div class="reveal">
        <h2 class="t-display">Let an agent drive it. Under guardrails.</h2>
        <p class="t-body-lg mt-5 measure">
          Gargantua ships a local Model Context Protocol server, so Claude,
          Cursor, or Claude Code can scan and run cleanups for you, which no
          other cleaner on the Mac currently lets an agent do.
        </p>
        <p class="t-body mt-4 measure">
          The catch that makes it safe: tools are split into two registries.
          Read-only calls are always available. Destructive calls require an
          explicit grant, bearer-token auth, and per-client rate limits, and a
          <span class="text-protected">protected</span> item is rejected before the
          tool ever runs.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-7 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <div class="rounded-lg border border-edge-soft bg-surface-1 p-4">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-safe)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 12s3-7 10-7 10 7 10 7-3 7-10 7-10-7-10-7Z"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/></svg>
              <span class="t-caption font-mono uppercase tracking-wide text-safe">Read-only</span>
            </div>
            <ul class="mt-3 space-y-1.5">
              {readOnly.map((t) => (
                <li class="t-mono-data text-ink-2">{t}</li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-lg border border-edge-soft bg-surface-1 p-4">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-review)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 9v4M12 17h.01"/><path d="M10.3 3.9 1.8 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.7 3h17a2 2 0 0 0 1.7-3L13.7 3.9a2 2 0 0 0-3.4 0Z"/></svg>
              <span class="t-caption font-mono uppercase tracking-wide text-review">Destructive, gated</span>
            </div>
            <ul class="mt-3 space-y-1.5">
              {destructive.map((t) => (
                <li class="t-mono-data text-ink-2">{t}</li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- agent session log -->
      <div class="reveal" style="--reveal-delay: 120ms">
        <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-edge bg-surface-1">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 border-b border-edge-soft px-4 py-2.5">
            <span class="flex gap-1.5" aria-hidden="true">
              <span class="h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-surface-4"></span>
              <span class="h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-surface-4"></span>
              <span class="h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-surface-4"></span>
            </span>
            <span class="t-caption font-mono">claude · gargantua-mcp</span>
            <span class="ml-auto inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 t-caption font-mono text-ink-3">
              <span class="inline-block h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-safe"></span>
              :7493
            </span>
          </div>

          <div class="space-y-3.5 px-5 py-5 font-mono text-[0.8125rem] leading-relaxed">
            <p class="text-ink-2">
              <span class="text-accent">agent</span> &gt; free up space from old build caches
            </p>

            <div class="rounded-md border border-edge-soft bg-surface-2 px-3.5 py-2.5">
              <p class="text-ink-3">
                <span class="text-safe">→ preview_cleanup</span>(profile: "dev-purge")
              </p>
              <p class="mt-1.5 text-ink-2">
                12 findings · <span class="text-ink">18.4 GB</span> reclaimable ·
                <span class="text-safe">safe</span>
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="rounded-md border border-edge-soft bg-surface-2 px-3.5 py-2.5">
              <p class="text-ink-3">
                <span class="text-review">→ run_cleanup</span>(scope: "dev-purge", confirm: true)
              </p>
              <p class="mt-1.5 text-ink-2">
                ✓ 18.4 GB moved to Trash · audit record written
              </p>
            </div>

            <div
              class="rounded-md border px-3.5 py-2.5"
              style="border-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-protected) 40%, transparent); background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-protected) 9%, transparent)"
            >
              <p class="text-ink-3">
                <span class="text-protected">→ run_cleanup</span>(path: "~/Library/Keychains")
              </p>
              <p class="mt-1.5 text-protected">
                ✗ rejected · path is <span class="font-semibold">protected</span>, not removable by any caller
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="t-caption mt-3 text-ink-3">
          The protected-roots policy is bundled and deterministic, so the same
          rejection applies whether the request comes from you or from a model.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
